Package: multimod
Title: Define and Render Mathematical Models Across Modeling Languages
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
  c(person(given = "Oleg", 
          family = "Lugovoy", 
          email = "olugovoy@optimalsolution.dev", 
          role = c("aut", "cre"), 
          comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5546-9875")))
Copyright: The example_models dataset contains content derived from energyRt,
    copyright the energyRt development team; see inst/COPYRIGHTS.
Description: A unified framework for mathematical model representation,
    analysis, transformation, and optimization. Uses a universal intermediate
    representation (IR) to construct, import, inspect, simplify, and export
    mathematical models independently of modeling languages and solvers.
    Supports 'GAMS', 'GNU MathProg', 'JuMP', 'Pyomo', and 'LaTeX', direct
    generation and reduction of linear programming (LP) matrices, solving
    with 'HiGHS', 'cuOpt', and solution decoding. Currently focused on
    continuous linear optimization.
URL: https://optimal2050.github.io/multimod/, https://github.com/optimal2050/multimod
